---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, hrefEn as href } from '../../../lib/site';

const enlace = 'text-tinta underline decoration-oro/50 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-oro-oscuro';
const parrafo = 'mt-4 text-[16px] text-pizarra';
const titulo = 'mt-3 font-display text-[clamp(21px,2.2vw,27px)] font-semibold leading-[1.2]';
const numero = 'font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-oro-oscuro';
const lista = 'mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[16px] text-pizarra marker:text-oro-oscuro';

const navegadores = [
  { nombre: 'Google Chrome', url: 'https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647' },
  { nombre: 'Mozilla Firefox', url: 'https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/delete-cookies-remove-info-websites-stored' },
  { nombre: 'Safari', url: 'https://support.apple.com/en-us/guide/safari/sfri11471/mac' },
  {
    nombre: 'Microsoft Edge',
    url: 'https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="This website does not set its own cookies. Analytics are anonymous and cookieless; the Google calendar on the contact page is only loaded, and may set its own cookies, if you choose to display it."
>
  <section class="wrap pb-14 pt-20 md:pb-20 md:pt-28">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Legal</p>
    <h1
      class="mt-5 max-w-[16ch] font-display text-[clamp(38px,6vw,76px)] font-extralight leading-[1.04] tracking-[-0.035em]"
      data-reveal
    >
      No first-party cookies. Third parties kept to a minimum.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-[52ch] text-[clamp(17px,1.6vw,20px)] text-pizarra" data-reveal>
      This website does not set its own cookies. Visitor analytics are anonymous, aggregated and cookieless. The
      only exception is the Google booking calendar on the contact page, which is only loaded, and can only set its own
      cookies, if you click the button to display it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="hairline">
    <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
      <article class="max-w-[68ch] space-y-14">
        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>01</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>What are cookies?</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            Cookies are small text files that a website stores on your device when you
            visit it. They are used to remember preferences, maintain sessions or measure how the site is used.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>02</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Which cookies and technologies do we use?</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            No first-party cookies. This website is static, requires no login or user session
            and sets no first-party cookies. We also do not use Google Analytics, social media pixels
            or advertising or cross-site tracking tools.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            To see which pages are visited we use Umami, an analytics tool that sets no
            cookies, does not store the IP address and does not identify the visitor. It only records
            aggregated data: page viewed, country, device type and source of the visit. It runs on our
            own server, at stats.77delta.com, within the European Union.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The contact form sends your message to api.77delta.com, our own subdomain with
            infrastructure in the European Union. It does not set cookies either.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            To remember whether you prefer to view the website in Spanish, Catalan or English, we store a value in the
            browser's local storage (<code>localStorage</code>), not in a cookie. It is not sent to
            any server, does not expire on its own and you can delete it from your browser settings. It is a
            strictly necessary technical mechanism for the language selector to work, equivalent to
            a cookie exempt from consent.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The only exception is the Google appointment booking calendar, on the <a
              href={href('/contacto/')}
              class={enlace}>contact page</a
            >. It is the only element on this site that we do not control, and it is not loaded by default: instead
            you will see a "Show calendar" button and a link to open it in a separate tab. Until
            you click that button, nothing is downloaded from Google. If you click it, Google may set its own
            cookies for the calendar to work and to prevent abuse; these are non-exempt third-party
            cookies, and that click is your express consent to them. If you prefer not to give it, the
            same page offers the contact form and a direct link to the calendar in a separate tab, neither of which
            embeds anything. You can read Google's cookie policy at <a
              href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class={enlace}>policies.google.com/technologies/cookies</a
            >.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The links to LinkedIn and WhatsApp are external links, not embedded content: you only interact
            with those services if you click on them, and their own cookie and privacy policies then
            apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>03</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Why there is no cookie banner</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            A consent banner is mandatory when a site sets non-exempt cookies before the
            user decides. None of the services under our control, neither Umami analytics nor the
            contact form, sets any cookies, so there is nothing to ask your consent for.
          </p>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            The exception is the Google calendar described in the previous section, and it is already blocked
            by default: instead of a generic banner, the calendar is only loaded if you click the "Show
            calendar" button. That click serves the same purpose as a banner, asking your permission before Google
            sets anything, and it is your express consent to those specific cookies. If you do not click it, Google neither
            receives nor sets anything. If in the future we add other third-party content that requires non-exempt
            cookies, such as videos or other calendars, we will apply the same load-on-request
            approach or, where that is not possible, an equivalent prior-consent mechanism.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>04</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>How can you manage cookies?</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            You can configure your browser to accept, reject or delete cookies from any website.
            Each browser offers different options:
          </p>
          <ul class={lista}>
            {
              navegadores.map((n) => (
                <li>
                  <a href={n.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class={enlace}>
                    {n.nombre}
                  </a>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>05</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Changes to the policy</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            This policy may be updated. Any change will be reflected here, with the date of the last
            update at the foot of the page.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section data-reveal>
          <p class={numero}>06</p>
          <h2 class={titulo}>Contact</h2>
          <p class={parrafo}>
            For any question about cookies, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class={enlace}
              >{site.email}</a
            >. The processing of personal data is described in the <a
              href={href('/politica-privacidad/')}
              class={enlace}>privacy policy</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <p class="hairline pt-8 font-mono text-[12px] text-pizarra" data-reveal>
          Last updated: 28 September 2026
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
